    {
      "id": "claim_92d59c8136294f509b31c532b0d989ce",
      "statement": "The jsonKey/localKey split is deliberate: Redis-backed caches share one store, so their address (toJsonKey) must carry the full key configuration to keep differently-configured entries apart, while file-based caches isolate configurations per file via CacheParameter.parameters() and only need a stable content-derived handle (localKey) inside the file — the two keys are separate addresses for the same logical entry in the two storage worlds.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/edu/kit/kastel/mcse/ardoco/llm/cache/CacheKey.java#L30-L45",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9f1270cdce06f80ce9d67a24eedff5c9a0c5b9b9ebaac2d3b36d939cf95a62f3:"
        },
