    {
      "id": "claim_9133d70f9c4a4d9ab7d5926a1b73cb5f",
      "statement": "Cache.getViaInternalKey and Cache.putViaInternalKey are deprecated (forRemoval = false) methods that take the internal K key directly, bypassing content-based key derivation; their only legitimate users are the long-text embedding recovery path (CachedEmbeddingCreator.tryToFixWithLength reads and stores a truncated-prefix embedding under a custom local key built with the deprecated EmbeddingCacheKey.ofRaw) and layer conflict resolution (HierarchicalCache and CacheReplacementStrategy.resolveViaInternalKey copy/overwrite values between layers without access to the original content); they preserve the JSON-values invariant and mirror the content-string methods so CHAT and EMBEDDING keys never collide.",
      "evidence": [
